{"uid":"3fea7faf2f59839","name":"test_header_makes_no_self_skip_claim_about_the_docker_or_browser_tiers","fullName":"tests.test_host_like_pytest_script#test_header_makes_no_self_skip_claim_about_the_docker_or_browser_tiers","historyId":"09f1c033aaa21006ca19687a723451b5","time":{"start":1791921443470,"stop":1791921443476,"duration":6},"description":"F2 (#74): an earlier header claimed a usable docker socket is always\n    present here, so the docker tier is always filtered out and self-skip\n    is dismissed outright as a false premise -- itself false, since socket\n    presence genuinely varies per invocation (some ralphd job containers\n    have one, some -- including this one -- do not, and a bare developer\n    host usually has none). The header's actual, current behaviour branches\n    on that per-invocation probe: when a usable socket IS present it\n    injects ``-m \"not docker\"`` to filter the tier out (never runs it\n    nested); when the socket is ABSENT it injects nothing, and the\n    docker-marked modules' own module-level ``skipif`` self-skips cleanly,\n    the same as it would for a developer running the bare command by hand.\n    The header must describe *both* branches, cite #74, and must not claim\n    either branch -- present or absent -- as this environment's\n    unconditional, universal behaviour.","descriptionHtml":"<p>F2 (#74): an earlier header claimed a usable docker socket is always<br />\npresent here, so the docker tier is always filtered out and self-skip<br />\nis dismissed outright as a false premise -- itself false, since socket<br />\npresence genuinely varies per invocation (some ralphd job containers<br />\nhave one, some -- including this one -- do not, and a bare developer<br />\nhost usually has none). The header's actual, current behaviour branches<br />\non that per-invocation probe: when a usable socket IS present it<br />\ninjects <code>-m &quot;not docker&quot;</code> to filter the tier out (never runs it<br />\nnested); when the socket is ABSENT it injects nothing, and the<br />\ndocker-marked modules' own module-level <code>skipif</code> self-skips cleanly,<br />\nthe same as it would for a developer running the bare command by hand.<br />\nThe header must describe <em>both</em> branches, cite #74, and must not claim<br />\neither branch -- present or absent -- as this environment's<br />\nunconditional, universal behaviour.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791921443464,"stop":1791921443466,"duration":2},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791921443464,"stop":1791921443464,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_task_record_dir","time":{"start":1791921443466,"stop":1791921443466,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_scrub_notifier_env_in_process","time":{"start":1791921443467,"stop":1791921443468,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_stub_escalation_backoff_at_class_level","time":{"start":1791921443468,"stop":1791921443468,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_undo_instant_sleep_patches","time":{"start":17919